# Derived, multi-MB analysis outputs inside a batch archive. They are reproducible from the frozen
# snapshot by the tracked tools, so the archive keeps its EVIDENCE (RESULTS.md, corpus_manifest.json,
# runs.json, applicability.json, the guard transcripts) and not a 4 MB re-derivation: committing them
# made one round 155,906 inserted lines for a 5 MB artifact. acceptance_1.7.11 (round 6) predates this
# rule and stays complete as history; the files remain on disk either way.
/_dpsm_work/acceptance_*/pairtrusted_impact_report.json
/_dpsm_work/acceptance_*/pairtrusted_impact_report.txt

# Scratch files under tests/ (commit messages, throwaway harnesses). tests/ is re-included above, so
# without this rule a `git add -A` picks a temporary file up and the next commit deletes it again.
# R53: broadened from "_*.tmp" to "_*" -- AGENTS section 4 says scratch files live here, and trusting the
# suffix meant a "_census_r53.tmp.json" got committed (a .tmp stem with a .json tail). The rule now
# enforces itself; no tracked file under tests/ starts with an underscore.
/_dpsm_work/tests/_*

# --- derived output / caches, anywhere ---
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- heavy or volatile inputs and artefacts (recorded by hash, not tracked) ---
BepInEx/plugins/
BepInEx/interop/
BepInEx/core/
BepInEx/LogOutput.log
BepInEx/config/dpsmeter_runtime.log*
rlyehshoujotaix_cl_Data/
D3D12/
dotnet/
DpsMeter-0.9.0-r2/
姹夊寲/
*.zip
*.dll
*.exe
*.bak
